# `index.html` carries the inline theme script that the production
# Content-Security-Policy admits by hash, and a hash is over bytes. A CRLF
# working copy would therefore compute a different answer from the LF checkout
# the Mac Mini builds and serves. Pinning the endings keeps the one script that
# has to match byte-for-byte identical on every machine.
#
# See `deploy/macos/csp-hash.test.ts`.
index.html text eol=lf

# Shell scripts run on macOS. A CRLF checkout of these fails with an
# uninformative `bad interpreter` at the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/macos/Caddyfile text eol=lf
